2 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fredrik_Magnus_Piper
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fredrik Magnus Piper''' (1746–1824) was a Swedish landscape architect and architect. He introduced the theory and practice of the English landscape garden to Sweden.[1][2] Among his tangible contributions are the creation of th
2 CONC e general plan for the royal park Hagaparken in Stockholm, part of the current Royal National City Park, and contributions to the development of the park at Drottningholm Palace.
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fredrik_Magnus_Piper
