1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wikipedia (en): [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_Stiernstr%C3%A5le Magnus Stiernstråle]
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelsvapen wiki (sv): [http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stiernstr%C3%A5le_nr_571 Stiernstråle adliga ätten nr. 571]
2 CONT
2 CONT Kansallisbiografia (fi): [https://biografiasampo.fi/henkilo/p2304 Magnus Stiernstråle]
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Stiernstråle (died December 18, 1738) was a Swedish military colonel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stiernstråle became captain of the Hämeenlinna infantry in 1648. When the Great Northern War erupted in 1700, he was lieutenant colonel and commander of the Ivangorod Fortress, which he had to give up on August 16, 1704. In 1710 h
2 CONC e became a colonel in Vyborg and Commandant of the Vyborg Fortress, which was fitted with a garrison of only 4 000. In March, it was attacked by a numerically superior Russian force under General Fyodor Apraksin.
2 CONT
2 CONT At first, the Russians, who had not brought any real siege artillery, had little success. Soon, however, when Czar Peter I himself arrived on May 10 with reinforcements and supplies, they gained the upper hand. From this time, the
2 CONC y were besieged in a position more and more desperate, and in vain waited for rescue from the Finnish side. Since the city walls to a large extent been destroyed and the crew weakened by disease and suffering, Stiernstråle surrend
2 CONC ered on June 13, 1710. Although he was the commander of the defense forces, and much of the bourgeoisie were taken as prisoners to Russia, Stiernstråle was taken to Pinsgorod, from where he first after peace returned in 1721. He w
2 CONC as promoted to Major General in 1721, and in 1723 received command of the Savo Regiment.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
